Z||000000||Hank is Here||08-29-2001||11:17 PM||||I am considering upgrading the old 125C tranny to the 440t4/4L60.  <BR>Does a stock 2.8 and the above trannies mix well in the Fiero.  Basically will the 2.8 have enough torque (or a$$)  to operate the car comfortably at the lower RPM.  <BR>I want to know specifically for the 2.8, not the 3.1 or 3.4.  <P>When I search the boneyards, are the RPO codes the same for all GM products?  If for example would the GX3 code be the same in the Fiero and a Lumina?  or does this differ per car?  BTW the GX3 is a 3.33 final drive ratio.<P>Thanks <BR>Hank ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||08-30-2001||08:35 AM||||??||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||08-30-2001||10:52 AM||||Hank, I don't have that combo but wanted to say that no one (with a street car) has the 4L60 as the 'L' is for longitudinal.  Some people have gone to the 4 speeds on the forum so they can tell you more.  You also should ask a dealer to look-up different variations of a specific model/year and final drive ratios once you zero in on what you want to put in it.  That way you can match your engines powerband to the trans and your driving needs for better drivability. GL||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||08-30-2001||11:20 AM||||I'm resting before I put my 440T4/4T60 into my 86 SE w/3.2 (back is complaining so I had to stop for awhile.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>The transaxle came from an 89 Pontiac Grand Prix with a 2.8!!!<P>Since the factory put them together, I guess you can too!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||08-30-2001||11:29 AM||||Hank-<P>I am running the 440t 4Spd OD tranny.  Yes, I do have a 3.1L- but the engine isn't that much different powerwise.  The 2.8 would be great on the 440t.  I get better gas mileage, especially on long trips.  I don't have mine wired to lock up the torque-converter yet, so I cruise at 95-100mph at 3000 rpm in 4th- AND get nearly 40mpg over a good distance at that speed (traveling back from Dells Run this year).<P>{Oh, I see he already posted...}<P>Pherder (Paul) is currently working on installing the 440 into his car- you may want to check with him too (I'm not sure what engine he's doing...)  Let me know if you have any other questions!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
